T23:10:02.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/jacksonville-jaguars/post/_/id/31017/jacksonville-jaguars-nfl-draft-picks-2023-selection-analysis","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Michael DiRocco","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NFL reassigns backup refs to work games closer to home","description":"The NFL, trying to avoid further travel issues from Friday's FAA ground stop, has reassigned officials to Week 10 games within driving distance of their homes.","published":"2026-11-14T15:34:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50479995/nfl-reassigns-backup-refs-work-games-closer-home","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Vikings made initial Kirk Cousins trade call to Raiders before MNF","description":"The Vikings initially reached out to the Raiders about a Kirk Cousins trade before their MNF game against the Bills, sources told ESPN and NFL Network.","published":"2026-11-14T15:58:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50479874/sources-vikings-first-called-kirk-cousins-mnf","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Schefter and Ian Rapoport","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NFL Week 10 predictions: Upsets, fantasy sleepers, stat lines, TD scorers, more","description":"Touchdown for Chuba Hubbard? Fantasy upside for Aaron Rodgers? Trick play from the Raiders? Let's predict 15 things for Week 10.","published":"2026-11-14T11:53:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50453290/week-10-predictions-upsets-fantasy-sleepers-stats-2026","type":"Story","byline":"Matt Bowen, Pamela Maldonado, Eric Moody, Ben Solak and Seth Walder","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Falcons insist winning still the goal despite trading Jessie Bates III","description":"Atlanta wanted to ensure trading away Jessie Bates III didn't send the wrong message to the team.","published":"2026-11-14T11:00:03.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50473666/atlanta-falcons-trade-deadline-jessie-bates-morale","type":"Story","byline":"Marc Raimondi","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Why the Raiders named Fernando Mendoza as the starter","description":"The Raiders named Fernando Mendoza as the starter shortly after trading Kirk Cousins to the Vikings.","published":"2026-11-14T11:00:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50466331/las-vegas-raiders-why-fernando-mendoza-starting","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McFadden","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Untold stories of Detroit Lions WR Amon-Ra St. Brown's German upbringing","description":"For Amon-Ra St. Brown, Sunday's NFL game in Munich will mark the ultimate convergence of his dual heritage. Here are stories that shed more light.","published":"2026-11-14T11:00:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50475710/nfl-germany-lions-amon-ra-st-brown-munich","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Despite Cousins trade, are Vikings back to square one at QB?","description":"Cousins can give some short-term relief, but his future and the search for a franchise QB remain uncertain.","published":"2026-11-14T11:00:01.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50472099/vikings-kirk-cousins-trade-contract","type":"Story","byline":"Kevin Seifert","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Patriots are 6-0 after a regular-season loss under Vrabel: Can they do it again?","description":"New England plays in Munich, Germany, this week. Catch up on what's happening abroad in this week's Patriots notebook.","published":"2026-11-14T13:32:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50475264/patriots-lions-germany-week-10-mike-vrabel","type":"Story","byline":"Mike Reiss","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Seahawks are hurting with injuries, but two players will return vs. Raiders","description":"QB Drew Lock will start again for Darnold. And LB Uchenna Nwosu and WR Rashid Shaheed will return to the field in Las Vegas.","published":"2026-11-14T04:01:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50475505/seahawks-raiders-week-10-darnold-lock-shaheed-returns","type":"Story","byline":"Brady Henderson","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Tyler Lacy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyler_Lacy","description":"American football player (born 1999)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:35:11Z","intro":"Tyler Lacy (born November 10, 1999) is an American professional football defensive tackle for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Oklahoma State Cowboys. Lacy was selected by the Jacksonville Jaguars in the fourth round of the 2023 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Lacy was born on November 10, 1999, in Garland, Texas. He is a cousin of former National Football League (NFL) player Aaron Ross, a Super Bowl champion with the New York Giants. He attended Sachse High School, being a consensus three-star recruit, and committed to play college football at Oklahoma State after his graduation from the school."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As freshman in 2018, Lacy redshirted and saw no game action at Oklahoma State. The following year, he started all 10 games in which he appeared, missing three due to injury, totaling 20 tackles, including two for a loss, with one sack and two pass breakups. In 2020, he remained a starter and was named honorable mention all-conference after leading the team's defensive line with 32 tackles and eight TFLs, additionally posting four sacks and five quarterback hurries.\nLacy earned a second honorable mention all-conference selection in 2021, additionally being named to their first-team All-Academic squad as he posted 34 tackles, 11 for-loss, and 3.5 sacks. He also recorded eight hurries, the fifth-best in school history since they started tracking the statistic in 1982. His senior season in 2022 was cut short due to injury, and he finished it with 17 tackles, five quarterback hits and three sacks. Lacy finished his stint at Oklahoma State with 113 tackles, 30 for-loss and 11.5 sacks while appearing in 44 total games."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"JACKSONVILLE JAGUARS\nLacy was selected by the Jacksonville Jaguars in the fourth round (130th overall) of the 2023 NFL draft. He appeared in 15 games and posted 12 tackles and a pass deflection in his first season.\nOn August 26, 2025, Lacy was waived by the Jaguars as part of final roster cuts.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn August 27, 2025, Lacy was claimed off waivers by the Detroit Lions."}],"wikidataId":"Q117716061","family":[{"relation":"Relative","name":"Aaron Ross","description":"American football player (born 1982)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_Ross"}],"social":{"x":"tylerlacy85","instagram":"tylerlacy85"}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361861","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/L/LacyTy00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/tyler-lacy/76836","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/tyler-lacy/10954","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyler_Lacy"},"insights":["On the field for 33% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.1M is the 37th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Drafted 130th overall in 2023 (round 4) by JAX."]}